# Caduceus Port to Olympus OM-D E-M1 Mark II (v3.70): Status & TODO

Updated 2026-11-10 (after the v0.2b1 camera test). Addresses and evidence: em1mk2/docs/ARCHITECTURE_AND_MEMORY_MAP.md §6–7,
em1mk2/docs/REA_FIRMWARE_FUNCTIONS_REFERENCE.md §1, docs/PORT_EM1MK2.md §4, WORKLOG.md (2026-11-10).

---

## 1. What exists

### A. Firmware container & build tooling
* Target: E-M1 Mark II fw 3.70 (build 3700, model 0x1250), MN10300 / AM33-2, main base VMA 0x60021020.
* 5-component 93 MB container rebuilt by tools/build_package.py; edits verified against stock bytes.
* Releases: v0.1, v0.2b1, v0.2b2 (camera-tested, looks wrong), v0.3b1 (built, NOT camera-tested).
  `python3 tools/omdem1mk2_make_release_edits.py <VERSION>` rebuilds patches and seals a release in its own folder.

### B. Working on camera (v0.1)
* rec_limit (29 min / 2 h → 9 h), focus_stacking (lens whitelist removed).

### C. SD card look loader (sd_loader)
* Cave 0x60580200 (Section 2), trigger at TRIG1 half-press classifier 0x6023d0db.
* Reads EM1MOD/LOOKS.BIN (2,080 B: 32 B header 'EM1B' + 16 × 128 B slots), CRC-32 check.
* Owns the shared state block P (patches/omdem1mk2/p_layout.inc): p_get / p_ensure, handle u16 at 0x621e24ae.
* Slot = shared Caduceus 64 B lookRecord (webapp/src/format.ts) + E-M1 extras: +64 vividness, +65 hue.

### D. Color Creator look editor (color_creator_wheel), v0.2b1
* Editor record 0x61259c40 (key 0x13a9), cave 0x612e6900 (1,944 B), guide label .data init word 0x60297fb4,
  SCP cell call 0x60e25ec8.
* Writes: hue 617 (0..29), vividness 618 (-4..+3), tone 889/890/891 (HL/MID/SH, order inferred from E-P7),
  all through facade SetValue(sid, 0, v) = the call the stock Color Creator commit 0x60e4c0a7 makes.
* Page 1 Chroma is shown but NOT applied. Banner shows " Exx" if a 617/618 write fails.

---

## 2. Camera issues and what caused them

v0.2b1 report (2026-11-10): saturation always 0; looks all look the same; garbage look names;
hue/saturation/chroma do nothing.

**Main cause (v0.1 and v0.2b1):** all patch state lived at 0x621e2f76..0x621e2f87, inside a stock
32-entry {callback, argument} ring at 0x621e2f74 (drained by 0x6023d1cb, which calls each entry).
Stock overwrote our card flag, buffer pointer, look index, page and dial flag, causing the garbage
names, looks not sticking and wrong pages. We overwrote queued callbacks. The "unreferenced .bss"
claim only checked absolute addresses. Fixed in v0.2b2: heap block P + validated u16 handle at
0x621e24ae (alignment padding; statically checked, camera-unproven).

Also fixed in v0.2b2: sd_check had no call slot (could corrupt the caller's saved a2 = buffer);
loader free was the uncached-pool free; names are filtered to printable ASCII.

Fixed in v0.2b1 (still valid): E-P7 sid numbers (this body = E-P7 minus 2), d2/d3 clobbered in the
arrow/dial handlers, vividness -5, untraced commit/refresh calls, card generator writing sat over
the tone bytes. SetValue has no "mode filter" (it rejects only on global busy bits).

"Saturation always 0": the Chroma page is intentionally not applied yet (P3 below). If the stock
wheel's vividness also stays 0, that is a separate symptom.

## 2b. v0.3b1 (2026-11-10): E-P7 colour route
* Colour stage = E-P7/PEN-F (selector 0x603ec82c, builder 0x603ec642). Hooks in the Section 2 cave:
  cc_sel at 0x603ec89b (CC + active look -> S into request+1816, COLOR branch), cc_hl at 0x603ec8b8
  (E-P7 `lv` H/L). Gate: live raw 0x9481 == value recorded when the CC editor opened.
* EM1MOD/LOOKS.BIN = E-P7 v3 file (Control Panel em1mk2 target now = shared encoder; byte-identical).
* P uncached (0x6002329a). Chroma page now offsets all 12 sectors.
* Banner diag: " K<hex key>" (+ "+" once applied). Test list in docs/PORT_EM1MK2.md.

## 2c. v0.3b1 camera result (2026-11-11) -> v0.3b2
* Colours change (COLOR engine route confirmed working). Only 2 labels / 2-3 distinct looks: the built-in
  looks were past the real Section 6 end 0x612e7000 (the docs' 0x61300000 was Section 7's start). Same bug
  hid preset tables in v0.1-v0.2. Fixed: built-ins in the Section 5 tail 0x60bc8150; check_loaded.py gates
  every release. Card not loading: banner now shows " C1/C0/CF".
* CC cave has 8 bytes left in Section 6: next features go to the S3/S4/S5 tails (code may call earlier sections).

## 2d. Upstream v0.31c merged (2026-11-11): what matters for this port
* AGENTS.md now requires ports to keep the shared look format/share codes/panel (we do: E-P7 LOOKS.BIN v3),
  to keep **firmware in its own repo**, and to contact @cakelesscoder (issue/PR) to merge the panel export
  target. To do once v0.3 works on camera: move em1mk2/ firmware to its own repo; offer
  webapp/src/targets/em1mk2.ts + the cameras.ts profile upstream.
* Look format: LOOKS.BIN unchanged (v3). New bytes are BUNDLES.BIN slot fields only (Sharp +51, Halo +52).
* docs/PORT_EM5III.md: E-M5 III also uses base 0x60021020 and the same 12-byte section records, which matches
  our E-M1 II section table (0x60027450).
* For later features: hardware watchdog (v0.31b raised it 10 s -> 30 s for CPU grain/halation; yields crashed);
  grain/halation untested with RAW+JPEG (docs/GRAIN_PORT.md). Flat profile lead in docs/UNLOCK_LEADS.md.

## 2e. v0.3b2 camera result (2026-11-11) -> v0.3b3
* Colours change better. B&W look's vividness -4 stuck for all looks (colour looks never reset 618; CC's own
  processing still runs on top). Only hue had an effect: tone wrote 889-891, which are dead on this body.
* v0.3b3: colour looks set 618 = 0; tone -> 449 (HL) / 450 (SH) (descriptor callbacks 0x602db1b2/0x602db195);
  Midtones page removed (no Midtone control on the E-M1 II); INFO cycles 3 pages.
* Open: CC hue still tints looks (find CC's neutral hue or bypass CC's stage); confirm HL/SH not swapped.

## 2f. v0.3b3 camera result (2026-11-11) -> v0.3b4
* B&W bug gone; looks change colour but subtly; Chroma/Luminance manual steps show no effect.
* v0.3b4: lv_refresh (re-write 618 current value) after manual steps; Strength page (x1..x3; S <= +-10,
  H/L <= +-15); look_fill moved to the Section 2 cave (0x60580622). Section 2 cave 1,248 B.

## 2g. v0.3b4 camera (2026-11-11)
* Velvia JPEG ~ Panel preview (first camera confirmation of a look end to end, stills included). Blues a bit
  more cyan: check Provia on the same scene to separate the look from CC's hue / the monitor.
* v0.3b4 pages: Strength works; Chroma works (+5 visibly punchier; single steps subtle); Luminance: values stored
  (449/450 read back) but no visible effect. Pending: Test B JPEGs (H 0/S 0 vs H -7/S +7); LV vs JPEG for Chroma.
* Desk test (neutral / Provia / Velvia JPEGs): CC base ~ neutral (no compensation); Velvia +10..14 S at x1 = as
  designed. 449/450 swap: unknown (the earlier hint came from an unreliable patch). Check Page 2: front dial must move
  only bright areas, rear dial only dark ones; if reversed, swap the sids.

## 2h. v0.3b4 Test B (2026-11-11) -> v0.3b5
* 449/450 at 0/0, +5/+5, -5/-5: no change in live view or JPEG. v0.3b5 writes the request-side tone 384 (HL) /
  692 (MID) / 383 (SH), same keys and mapping as the E-P7; midtones from looks come back.
* CAMERA OK (v0.3b5): +7/+7 vs -7/-7 moves highlights (+14) and shadows (+24), mids +3, live view and JPEG.
* HL/SH order confirmed on camera (Highlights dial = bright areas only).
* Remaining: Provia vs Velvia back to back (same light, x1, Chroma 0) + Natural; then Velvia vs Panel.

## 2i. v0.4 camera result (2026-11-11) -> v0.4b1 / v0.4b2
* CAMERA (v0.4 = v0.3b5 + debug_log + aspect): the camera restarts at the shutter, no CADLOG.TXT, no Panorama/Wide in
  the menu.
* Restart = debug_log, two independent faults, each enough to crash at the first TRIG event (with or without DEBUG.TXT):
  call/ret frames did not match (do_debug_log `call [d2,d3,a2,a3],36` / `ret [],4`; helpers `[],0` / `ret [],4`),
  and it stored its flags into its own Section 4 cave (loaded image: FIRMWARE_GUIDE §10 lesson 2). The opcode audit
  checked neither. Fixed in v0.4b1 (state in P+96..103, mount gate, matched frames); the audit now fails on both.
* Aspect: no static cause found. Validator 270, menu {270,6→8}, SCP {270,5→7} all patched like E-P7 v4+; all edits
  in loaded sections; sids 511/512 share the stock list but the E-P7 has the same records and worked. Untested,
  because the shutter crash came first.
* v0.4b1 on camera: still restarts. Third fault: the hook jmp landed one byte before the cave, on an 0xFF `break`
  (displacement from addr+1). v0.4b1/b2 withdrawn; check_loaded now verifies hook targets.
* v0.4b3 on camera: CARD error every half-press (with DEBUG.TXT); without it live view resets, nothing captured.
  Hook site 0x6023d10a (join of every path, no HLS_EVENT task gate) is the suspect. Logger pulled from releases.
* ROOT CAUSE (emulated): interlock rule record 179 value tables (1,3,2,4,9,10 only) → facade +36 rejects 6/7.
* DONE v0.4c1 on camera: Panorama selectable (strip), 5184x1920 JPEG. Menu option list lacks rows; strip cells blank.
* DONE v0.4c3 on camera: menu row "65:24"/"21:9"; detail screen 2 empty selectable entries (vanish after scrolling past);
  SCP missing. Full write-up: docs/OMD-EM1-II/ASPECT.md.
* DONE v0.4c5 on camera: regular menu works great; SCP shows 65:24 / 21:9 selectable but BLANK (0x1ff/0x200 lists = SCP
  source; icons appended after OSD resource 69 don't draw).
* DONE v0.4c6 on camera: SCP still blank; AF selector in 6/7 = 4:3 layout, no cursor, AF works.
* DONE v0.4c7 on camera: SCP 65:24 and 21:9 (stock 16:9 pointer) both blank; AF same as c6. → cell index miss (emulated).
* RULE: emulate every change before a camera build (AGENTS.md). Harnesses: tools/omdem1mk2_emu_scp.py, _emu_af.py.
* DONE v0.4c13 [C]: SCP tile + option row show 65:24 / 21:9; AF selector works (since c8); regular menu works.
* DONE v0.4c13-sp1 [C]: S+ after bursts / modes -> 0x612e7000..0x61300000 (100 KB) usable. S+ also after a power cycle and a movie.
* DONE v0.4c14 [C]: C0.0 -> the hook site 0x6023d0db never runs on a half-press (wrong site since v0.1).
* DONE v0.4c15 [C]: C1.1 after a half-press: LOOKS.BIN loads (hook 0x602f7bf7). To confirm: card look names / colours.
* NOW: halation step 2: spare remembered setting for the stage; Soft Focus / CPU-pass sites (code-shape search).
* NEXT FEATURE: halation (E-P7 version), global over any film / colour profile. Plan and owner decisions:
  docs/OMD-EM1-II/HALATION.md. Step 1 = code space, step 2 = spare remembered setting + Soft Focus / CPU-pass sites.
* NEXT (aspect, untested): live-view framing, rec-view, power-cycle with 6/7 saved, RAW+JPEG, Live Control strip,
  remaining E-P7 AF sites (tracking/AUTO), grid overlay. Then decide whether to bring debug_log back.
* Trace later: what uses RAM 0xa3b0e400..0xa3bb7140 after OSD bank 69 (why the append drew blank).
* Then: AF target selector with 65:24/21:9, live-view framing, power-off/on with 6/7 saved.
* NEXT: real 65:24 / 21:9 icons (OSD component 0x101, E-P7 patches/aspect/osd_icons.py route).
* (old) flash v0.4c1 (text strip labels) → Menu 1 > Image Aspect and SCP/Live Control should list Panorama + Wide.
  If the strip cells are blank: v0.4c2 (placeholder icons). Then real XP/21:9 icons + menu label text.
* (old) v0.3b5r (== camera-tested v0.3b5) to recover; v0.4b5 (v0.3b5 + aspect only).
* Logger later: E-M1 II HLS tid + task proof, then re-site with the E-P7/OM-3 four-part gate.
* (old) flash v0.4b3 (no aspect). Shutter must work; with DEBUG.TXT, CADLOG.TXT must appear. Then v0.4b4 (+ aspect):
  Shooting Menu 1 > Image Aspect and the SCP aspect strip; note blank rows vs no rows.

## 3. TODO

### Priority 1: Camera test v0.3b2 (docs/PORT_EM1MK2.md §4 "Camera test for v0.3b1")
0. Half-press once after power-on, open Color Creator: readable names?
1. Page 0 look step: does the reticle move and the image change? Any " Exx" code?
2. After picking Velvia (H+1 M0 S-4), does the stock Highlight & Shadow screen show it, in that order?
   This confirms or rejects 889/890/891 and their order.
3. Page 2/3 banners follow the dials? (They are read back from the settings.)
4. Multi-detent dial turns now step more than once?
5. SCP tile: does the rear dial change the live view or the icon while the text stays on the look name?

### Priority 2: Decide from the test
* If " E58": find what sets the busy bits (0x607abb14) while the editor is open, and defer the write
  (e.g. do it from the child commit path instead of the key handler).
* If " E16": dump the value we pass vs the child's list (+104) for that sid.
* If no code but still no image change: the write succeeds and something reverts it. Check the editor's
  cancel/restore path and whether 617/618 are snapshotted on entry.
* If tone lands in the wrong slot: try 449/450 and the mirrors 383 (SH) / 384 (HL) / 692 (MID).

### Priority 3: next E-P7 features on the colour route (after v0.3b1 works)
* Tone Blacks/Whites: locate the E-P7 `tone` site (0x603b14ff) here; mono looks (B&W path);
  stills vs live view check; persistence of the picked look across power-off.

### (done in v0.3b1) port the E-P7 colour route instead of Color Creator values
* Found: this body has the E-P7/PEN-F COLOR engine (selector 0x603ec82c, builder 0x603ec642, hook site
  0x603ec8b3 byte-identical to E-P7 0x603b02d9), gated on job key 11.
* Copy the E-P7 movie layer design (docs/MOVIE_COLOUR.md "As built"): job key -> 11 when a look is active,
  effective-S reads -> look S, 0xF6B1 message byte non-zero; then H/L at 0x603ec8b3 like the E-P7 `lv` hook.
* Read LOOKS.BIN in the E-P7 container so both cameras share one file.

### Priority 3b (old plan): 12-sector saturation
* Read-site override at the builder's 0xF6EA reads (0x602d24fb..0x602d25db, getter 0x6005e6cf):
  when picture mode = Color Creator and a look is active, return the look's sector values.
  Same technique as the E-P7 NR override (docs/FIRMWARE_GUIDE.md).
* First check: does the pipeline use request +24208 outside picture mode 11? An emulator run of the
  builder or a camera A/B with an extreme value.
* Also find the capture-side copy (0x60cc1f.. fills the same offsets for the mirrors; check for 0xF6EA there).

### Priority 4: SCP tile
* Show "look name" only when 617/618 still equal the look's values; otherwise show the stock text.
* Confirm by camera first (Priority 1 item 5).

### Priority 5: Consolidated Caduceus for E-P7 + E-M1 II
* One Control Panel: the em1mk2 target already exports the shared lookRecord. Add +64/+65
  (vividness/hue) mapping from the look's colour data so panel-made cards get a Color Creator base too.
* Feature map E-P7 → E-M1 II (each needs its own hook on this body; nothing is copied by address):
  - Film looks: hue/vivid/tone now; per-sector sat next (P3); per-sector hue/light needs a request field
    (look for the E-P7 COLOR table equivalent in TruePic VIII).
  - Mono looks: Color Creator cannot do B&W. Options: switch picture mode 111 to Monotone for mono looks
    (leaves Color Creator) or a request-level override.
  - Grain, sharpening off, NR per look: E-P7 hooks are CPU-side save paths; find E-M1 II equivalents.
  - Aspect ratios, button functions: list-table edits; repeat the stride search on this body.
* Keep each body's firmware in its own patch folder; share only the look format and the panel.
